; minishop.rules — questions about the failure space, as relations.
;
; Read by `writ derive`. A rule never adds a situation, an edge or a cell;
; it only names a set the interrogator already computed, so nothing here
; can change what the model means.
;
; `holds` does not bind its situation, so each rule ranges over `situation`
; first — a body joins in written order (writ interrogator, extension §4).

; The configurations where the store's connection pool is exhausted.
; In the drifted model these are exactly the situations that `healthy:`
; calls fine and the state rules call `saturated` — the contradiction,
; named and listed rather than counted.
(relation saturated 1)
(rule (saturated S)
  (situation S)
  (holds S (and (is store.available yes)
                (is store.connection-count at-or-above-500))))

; Situations from which the api can still be lost. The recursion walks
; BACKWARD from the goal, one pass over the edges; written forwards through
; a transitive closure it is the same set at a quadratic price.
(relation can-lose-api 1)
(rule (can-lose-api S)
  (situation S)
  (holds S (is api.reachable no)))
(rule (can-lose-api S)
  (edge E S T)
  (can-lose-api T))
